Whitelist::constructor(address _registry)
├── Given _registry is the zero address
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientZeroRegistry
└── Given _registry is non-zero
    └── It should set up the EIP-712 domain (name "EverStratWhitelist", version "1")

Whitelist::isWhitelisted(address _user)
├── Given disabled() is true
│   └── It should return true for every address (including previously banned ones —
│       disable() opens the protocol; ban state is ignored for entry)
└── Given disabled() is false
    ├── Given _user is banned
    │   └── It should return false (regardless of local whitelist state)
    ├── Given _user is not banned and is locally whitelisted
    │   └── It should return true
    └── Given _user is not banned and is not locally whitelisted
        └── It should return false

Whitelist::whitelist(address _user, bytes32 _inviteId, uint256 _deadline, bytes calldata _signature)
├── Given the gate is disabled
│   └── It should return without reverting (no-op via isWhitelisted == true; invite left unconsumed)
├── Given _user is already whitelisted (isWhitelisted(_user) == true)
│   ├── It should return without reverting (no-op)
│   ├── It should NOT mark _inviteId as used
│   └── It should NOT emit UserWhitelisted
├── Given _user is not whitelisted and is banned
│   └── It should revert with WhitelistUserBanned (a stale unconsumed voucher cannot undo a ban)
├── Given _user is not whitelisted and not banned
│   ├── When _inviteId has already been used
│   │   └── It should revert with WhitelistInviteAlreadyUsed
│   ├── When block.timestamp is greater than _deadline
│   │   └── It should revert with WhitelistSignatureExpired
│   ├── When the signature is malformed (wrong length)
│   │   └── It should revert (ECDSA error)
│   ├── When the signature recovers to an address that is not an authorized signer
│   │   └── It should revert with WhitelistInvalidSignature
│   └── When the signature recovers to an authorized signer and the voucher is unexpired and unused
│       ├── It should mark _inviteId as used (isInviteUsed(_inviteId) == true)
│       ├── It should mark _user as whitelisted (isWhitelisted(_user) == true)
│       ├── It should emit UserWhitelisted(_user, _inviteId, block.timestamp)
│       ├── It should bind the signature to _user (a voucher signed for one user cannot whitelist another)
│       ├── It should bind the signature to this contract and chain (EIP-712 domain separator)
│       └── Given the caller is not _user (permissionless relaying)
│           └── It should still succeed and whitelist _user (not msg.sender)
└── Given the same voucher is replayed after _user is already whitelisted
    ├── It should return without reverting (no-op, not WhitelistInviteAlreadyUsed)
    └── It should NOT re-emit UserWhitelisted

Whitelist::addToWhitelist(address[] _users)
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── Given the gate is already disabled
│   └── It should revert with WhitelistIsDisabled (admin whitelisting is meaningless once open)
└── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE and the gate is still active
    ├── When _users contains the zero address
    │   └── It should revert with WhitelistZeroAddress
    └── When all addresses are valid
        ├── It should whitelist every address (isWhitelisted() == true for each)
        ├── It should emit UserWhitelistedByAdmin for each address
        └── Given an address was previously banned via removeFromWhitelist
            ├── It should clear isBanned for that address
            ├── It should make isWhitelisted return true
            └── It should allow a later voucher redeem (no WhitelistUserBanned)

Whitelist::removeFromWhitelist(address _user)
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── Given the gate is already disabled
│   └── It should revert with WhitelistIsDisabled (banning after open is meaningless)
└── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE and the gate is still active
    ├── It should clear local whitelisted state for _user
    ├── It should set _user as banned for the invite period (isBanned(_user) == true)
    ├── It should emit UserRemovedFromWhitelist
    ├── It should make isWhitelisted(_user) return false while the gate is active
    ├── Given disable() is later called
    │   └── It should make isWhitelisted(_user) return true (pre-disable bans no longer gate entry)
    └── Given a previously-unconsumed voucher exists for _user
        └── It should still revert with WhitelistUserBanned if later redeemed via whitelist()
            while the gate is still active

Whitelist::addSigner(address _signer)
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── Given the gate is already disabled
│   └── It should revert with WhitelistIsDisabled (invite signing is meaningless once open)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE and the gate is still active
│   ├── When _signer is the zero address
│   │   └── It should revert with WhitelistZeroAddress
│   ├── When _signer is already an authorized signer
│   │   └── It should revert with WhitelistSignerAlreadyAdded
│   └── When _signer is new and non-zero
│       ├── It should set isSigner(_signer) to true
│       └── It should emit SignerAdded(_signer)
└── Given caller has SECURITY_ROLE only (not ADMIN_ROLE)
    └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole (adding a signer is fail-closed: ADMIN-only, 48h timelock)

Whitelist::removeSigner(address _signer)
├── Given caller has neither ADMIN_ROLE nor SECURITY_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientCallerHasNoneOfRoles
├── Given the gate is already disabled
│   └── It should revert with WhitelistIsDisabled (signer management is meaningless once open)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE and the gate is still active
│   ├── When _signer is not currently authorized
│   │   └── It should revert with WhitelistSignerNotFound
│   └── When _signer is currently authorized
│       ├── It should set isSigner(_signer) to false
│       └── It should emit SignerRemoved(_signer)
└── Given caller has SECURITY_ROLE (no timelock) and the gate is still active
    ├── It should remove the signer immediately
    └── It should emit SignerRemoved(_signer)

Whitelist::disable()
├── Given caller does not have ADMIN_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole
├── Given caller has SECURITY_ROLE only (not ADMIN_ROLE)
│   └── It should revert with RegistryClientMissingRole (disabling the gate is a deliberate, timelocked product decision, not an emergency action)
├── Given caller has ADMIN_ROLE and the gate is not yet disabled
│   ├── It should set disabled() to true
│   ├── It should emit WhitelistDisabled
│   └── It should make isWhitelisted() return true for every address (including previously banned)
└── Given the gate is already disabled
    └── It should revert with WhitelistIsDisabled (irreversible, cannot be toggled back)
